.policy "ruff-d212-multi-line-summary-first-line" revision 2
.description "Start a multi-line docstring's summary right after the opening quotes, on the first line."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff D212 (pydocstyle): a multi-line docstring whose opening quotes stand alone on their line, so the summary
// starts on the second line. (D213 is the opposite convention.) Ruff tests the first line of the literal
// against the openers exactly: `"""` followed by spaces is not alone.
//   """
//   Summary.
//   """                      ← D212
#include "python/docstrings.rr"

.violation D212(at: node) code "D212"
    "Move this docstring's summary onto the line with the opening quotes, removing the line break after them."
    suppress ruff "D212"
D212(s) :- doc_checked(s), doc_triple(s), doc_body(s, b), match("\\r?\\n[\\s\\S]*", b).
